This moves the result from one selected contrast to the full scalar rank-one contrast class and gives a structural zero-gap/\(N^{-1}\)-gap elbow. It also transfers the finite-population correction to Gao–Ge–Qian’s arbitrary-\(K\) scalar contrast setting while remaining explicit that arbitrary \(d\) and general quadratic \(A\) achievability are not claimed.
